# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VMBS Branch Defects & Operational Standard Tracker — environment configuration
# Copy to .env.local for local dev; set these in Vercel for deploys.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Secret used to sign the admin session cookie (any long random string).
# REQUIRED in production. Generate: openssl rand -base64 32
SESSION_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# Admin password for the Settings page. OPTIONAL — there is a built-in default
# ("pa55w0rd") so sign-in works with no configuration at all. Set this to override
# the default. Once an admin changes it in-app (Settings → Admin password), the
# new password is hashed (scrypt) and persisted to storage (admin-credentials.json)
# and takes precedence over this value.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me

# ── Vercel Blob storage ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN is injected automatically when you connect a Vercel Blob
# store to the project. With no token set, the app uses a local ./.data folder
# (dev only) so `next dev` works without cloud storage.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD) — "Sign in with Microsoft" (ADDITIVE, identity
# only). People sign in as themselves and are mapped to a role from their
# verified email. INERT UNTIL CONFIGURED: with the two AZURE_AD_* values unset,
# the Microsoft button is hidden and role/admin sign-in is exactly as before.
# SSO NEVER grants admin — admin stays behind the admin password.
# AZURE_AD_CLIENT_ID=
# AZURE_AD_CLIENT_SECRET=
# AZURE_AD_TENANT_ID=common
# (SESSION_SECRET signs the session cookie for both SSO and the role/admin login.)
#
# Role mapping:
#   SUPERVISOR_EMAILS    -> supervisor. Defaults to sanchia.henry@myvmgroup.com
#                           if unset. Comma-separated.
#   ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAIN -> any other account on this domain signs in as an
#                           inspector/officer (default myvmgroup.com; "none" off).
#   INSPECTOR_EMAILS     -> optional explicit inspector allowlist. Comma-separated.
# SUPERVISOR_EMAILS=
# ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAIN=myvmgroup.com
#
# Azure redirect URI to register: https://<your-host>/api/auth/microsoft/callback
